WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:03.690
- I paid $100 to look
at a stranger's junk.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.523
Whoa!

00:00:04.523 --> 00:00:05.829
(groaning)

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:08.412
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.076
- You can buy a junk drawer off of Ebay,

00:00:14.076 --> 00:00:16.924
it's just somebody's random
junk that they accumulated.

00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:18.817
Most people have a junk
drawer in their house,

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:20.856
it's a lot of really weird random things.

00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:23.602
I bought two different
junk drawers off of Ebay,

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:25.331
in case one of them sucks.

00:00:25.331 --> 00:00:28.248
This junk drawer was $114,

00:00:28.248 --> 00:00:29.605
which is an insane amount to pay.

00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:31.250
This one we 65.95.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.497
Can I look in your drawer?

00:00:32.497 --> 00:00:33.427
- Oh my god.

00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:34.748
- [Joanna] What's up
with this giant pencil?

00:00:34.748 --> 00:00:36.028
- [Co-Worker] It's a giant novelty pencil.

00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:37.667
- [Joanna] How much do you
think someone would pay

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.630
for the stuff that's in your drawer?

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.929
- Probably like five bucks.

00:00:40.929 --> 00:00:42.334
- [Joanna] Can I look in your drawer?

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.993
Voodoo doll.

00:00:43.993 --> 00:00:45.378
- This is a pillow I cross stitched,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.331
it says Satan 666.

00:00:47.331 --> 00:00:49.538
- [Joanna] Do you think
someone would pay like $114

00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:51.173
for what you have in your drawer?

00:00:51.173 --> 00:00:52.855
- Oh no, Joanna are you doing that?

00:00:52.855 --> 00:00:54.566
- We're gonna see if we can find out

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:56.313
anything interesting about somebody

00:00:56.313 --> 00:00:58.593
based on what kind of
junk they've accumulated.

00:00:58.593 --> 00:01:01.790
Let's open up the slightly
less expensive junk drawer.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.280
Ooh, some of this looks like fancy junk.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.604
Whoa, okay this is a wooden
box and it's very heavy.

00:01:08.604 --> 00:01:12.104
And there's a real cool deer on the cover.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.948
Oh god, I thought it was locked,

00:01:14.948 --> 00:01:16.192
and I was gonna feel like an idiot

00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:19.407
if I got mailed a locked
box that I couldn't open.

00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:21.282
There's a lot of junk.

00:01:21.282 --> 00:01:23.503
Ooh, okay we have a pipe,

00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:25.025
we've got a baggie of coins,

00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:26.587
oh my god, I'm so gonna wear this.

00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:28.316
This is a bolo tie.

00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:29.514
There's a horse on it.

00:01:29.514 --> 00:01:32.456
My secret desire to be a cowboy
is about to be fulfilled.

00:01:32.456 --> 00:01:33.651
Bolo.

00:01:33.651 --> 00:01:35.848
Ooh, a pocket knife.

00:01:35.848 --> 00:01:37.867
Time for knifing.

00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:39.033
What is this?

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.559
I can't tell what it's made out of,

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:42.284
but it's getting all over me.

00:01:42.284 --> 00:01:44.092
The face is so scary.

00:01:44.092 --> 00:01:45.505
Nightmare bear.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.774
I feel like it's looking at me.

00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:48.124
It's like kind of broken.

00:01:48.124 --> 00:01:49.039
Oh god.

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:50.790
So this lighter says Dad on it.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.319
I've got your dad's lighter.

00:01:52.319 --> 00:01:54.524
This is the weirdest
coin I have ever seen.

00:01:54.524 --> 00:01:58.408
It says Zeus summons the Gods of Olympus.

00:01:58.408 --> 00:01:59.779
What?

00:01:59.779 --> 00:02:02.004
Is this something that
you shoot out of a gun?

00:02:02.004 --> 00:02:03.720
If babies drank beer,

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.900
I feel like they would
drink this baby beer.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.654
A tobacco container,

00:02:07.654 --> 00:02:10.387
with a very old-timey man on the front.

00:02:10.387 --> 00:02:13.575
This is the last thing that
came in this 65.95 box of junk.

00:02:13.575 --> 00:02:15.855
I don't know what this is.

00:02:15.855 --> 00:02:17.588
I can't tell if this is authentic or not.

00:02:17.588 --> 00:02:19.173
But this is an old whiskey bottle,

00:02:19.173 --> 00:02:20.681
it says Jack Daniel on it.

00:02:20.681 --> 00:02:22.369
Well I feel like this is the junk drawer

00:02:22.369 --> 00:02:26.086
of an old-timey grandfather cowboy man.

00:02:26.086 --> 00:02:29.195
I guess I have more knives
now than I did when I started,

00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:30.623
so that's exciting.

00:02:30.623 --> 00:02:33.004
I wish I had worn gloved
to go through this

00:02:33.004 --> 00:02:37.171
because now my hands are super
grimey with old-timey grime.

00:02:38.065 --> 00:02:39.283
It's not a great feeling.

00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:40.479
On to the next junk.

00:02:40.479 --> 00:02:44.017
This was the more expensive
junk drawer at $114.

00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:48.342
So let's see what $114
worth of junk looks like.

00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:49.483
(shouts)

00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:52.034
Okay this freaked me out

00:02:52.034 --> 00:02:55.428
because there's just
like a crumpled up body.

00:02:55.428 --> 00:02:56.669
This smells so musty.

00:02:56.669 --> 00:03:00.527
This is the hunchback of Notre Dame ...

00:03:00.527 --> 00:03:01.925
doll.

00:03:01.925 --> 00:03:03.791
This was like this in the box

00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:05.232
so it just looks like a headless doll.

00:03:05.232 --> 00:03:08.531
So there's these two purple mouse things,

00:03:08.531 --> 00:03:11.556
and they feel very dirty and old.

00:03:11.556 --> 00:03:13.208
They are so musty.

00:03:13.208 --> 00:03:14.805
Incense.

00:03:14.805 --> 00:03:15.722
Whoa, okay.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:18.634
This smells bad.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:21.139
This smells like a perfume
counter at a department store,

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:23.158
which to me is not super relaxing.

00:03:23.158 --> 00:03:26.903
This is an artist's
rendering of a football.

00:03:26.903 --> 00:03:29.942
I don't understand what this is.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:33.770
This is the fanciest
dolphin I've ever seen.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.198
This is most representative

00:03:35.198 --> 00:03:36.732
of what you find in a junk drawer.

00:03:36.732 --> 00:03:38.093
Just cords.

00:03:38.093 --> 00:03:41.457
We have a plastic coffin
that says RIP on it.

00:03:41.457 --> 00:03:43.267
This is a fun toy for
children to play with,

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.151
I don't know?

00:03:44.151 --> 00:03:46.517
This is a bracelet,

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:48.086
that doesn't quite close.

00:03:48.086 --> 00:03:49.765
I maybe broke this.

00:03:49.765 --> 00:03:51.084
This is a flashlight

00:03:51.084 --> 00:03:54.495
that says The Amazing
Live Sea Monkeys on it.

00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:58.418
So this is a sea monkey themed flashlight.

00:03:58.418 --> 00:04:02.190
Ooh, a membership card to
the Oasis Casino in Nevada.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.023
I just looked it up,

00:04:03.023 --> 00:04:04.561
this casino doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:04.561 --> 00:04:06.742
It was demolished in 2013.

00:04:06.742 --> 00:04:08.352
Ghost casino membership.

00:04:08.352 --> 00:04:10.734
After going through the
more expensive junk drawer,

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:11.744
I'm gonna be honest,

00:04:11.744 --> 00:04:14.524
I like kind of don't
care who this person was,

00:04:14.524 --> 00:04:17.462
it really just reminds
me that junk is terrible,

00:04:17.462 --> 00:04:19.895
one man's junk is another man's junk.

00:04:19.895 --> 00:04:21.192
I feel like somebody took this,

00:04:21.192 --> 00:04:22.785
and they held it up and they're like,

00:04:22.785 --> 00:04:24.861
does this give me joy, absolutely not.

00:04:24.861 --> 00:04:25.858
Which is understandable,

00:04:25.858 --> 00:04:27.504
this doesn't give me joy either.

00:04:27.504 --> 00:04:29.974
I feel happy that these people found a way

00:04:29.974 --> 00:04:31.218
to get rid of their junk.

00:04:31.218 --> 00:04:35.281
Now all I wanna do is just get
all the junk out of my life.

00:04:35.281 --> 00:04:37.527
I just super wanna go
wash my hands right now.

00:04:37.527 --> 00:04:38.993
Do you have a junk drawer Chelsea?

00:04:38.993 --> 00:04:40.056
- I did, I just went through it

00:04:40.056 --> 00:04:41.904
and then I put it in the
trash where it belongs.

00:04:41.904 --> 00:04:43.104
It still has junk it it,

00:04:43.104 --> 00:04:45.030
but it's my junk.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.363
But should I take this out of
the trash and sell it on Ebay?

00:04:47.363 --> 00:04:48.196
- [Joanna] Yeah.

